#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""KD Premium Emoji Bot — single-file build.

Python 3.10+. Install: pip install pyTelegramBotAPI==4.37.1 emoji==2.16.0
Only TOKEN and ADMIN_ID below need your values; environment overrides work too.
Run from the existing directory containing bot.db, users.json and redeem.txt.
Channels, effects and visual options are controlled from Owner Panel.
Offline checks: python main.py --self-test

Native button styles: primary/blue, danger/red, success/green.
Yellow is a single yellow custom-emoji accent with the client default style.
Custom emoji availability and reactions remain subject to Telegram permissions.
UI text uses small caps; URLs, commands and code spans remain copyable.
The start popup is a temporary emoji message that is deleted before welcome.
No user database is deleted or reset. First migration creates a SQLite backup.

UBUNTU / TERMIUS
1. Stop the old bot through its existing terminal/session/service.
2. Put this file in the existing folder containing bot.db, users.json and
   redeem.txt. Keep those data files. Save the Python file as main.py.
3. Set TOKEN and ADMIN_ID below, or supply BOT_TOKEN and BOT_ADMIN_ID.
4. In that folder run:
       sudo apt update
       sudo apt install -y python3 python3-venv python3-pip screen
       python3 -m venv .venv
       .venv/bin/python -m pip install pyTelegramBotAPI==4.37.1 emoji==2.16.0
       .venv/bin/python -m py_compile main.py
       .venv/bin/python main.py --self-test
5. For an existing kd-emoji systemd service:
       sudo systemctl restart kd-emoji
       sudo systemctl status kd-emoji --no-pager
       sudo journalctl -u kd-emoji -n 50 --no-pager
   For a terminal session that survives disconnecting Termius:
       screen -S kd-emoji .venv/bin/python main.py
   Detach with Ctrl+A, then D. Reattach: screen -r kd-emoji
   Screen does not start after a VPS reboot; use a systemd service for that.

Fresh systemd setup, when no service exists (run inside the bot directory):
    task_bot_dir="$PWD"
    task_bot_user="$(id -un)"
    sudo tee /etc/systemd/system/kd-emoji.service >/dev/null <<EOF
    [Unit]
    Description=KD Premium Emoji Bot
    Wants=network-online.target
    After=network-online.target
    [Service]
    User=$task_bot_user
    WorkingDirectory="$task_bot_dir"
    ExecStart="$task_bot_dir/.venv/bin/python" "$task_bot_dir/main.py"
    Environment=PYTHONUNBUFFERED=1
    Restart=on-failure
    RestartSec=5
    [Install]
    WantedBy=multi-user.target
    EOF
    sudo systemctl daemon-reload
    sudo systemctl enable --now kd-emoji
Remove the leading indentation when pasting the heredoc in a shell.

In Telegram: /start, then Owner Panel for Force Join and Effects & Theme.
The supplied 2,431 extra ID candidates are bundled; no IDs file is required.
Telegram validates them in the background using getCustomEmojiStickers.
Try all live media flows and channel permissions with your actual bot.
Offline checks use local API fakes and temporary data, not a live account.

Historical referral rewards cannot be reconstructed reliably. Existing users
are marked as processed during first migration; new verified referrals are
credited once. Lost in-memory posts from the original bot cannot be recovered.
"""
